WEBVTT

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.920
Tonight, I've come to Touto Tower in Minato Ward.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.210
Here at Touto Tower, the Tanabata Fair is currently underway.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.720
Many visitors have made their way here to...

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.590
I know.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.640
Meet at the professor's at 4:00 AM, right?

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.100
You too, Genta.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.510
Don't be late.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:40.060
Later.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.350
Now, I just need a flashlight.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.560
Let's see, I think...

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.900
I remember it being in this drawer.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:55.990
Got it.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.070
Who's there?

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.160
Ran-neechan?

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.000
Uncle's still out for mahjong, so it can't be him.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:12.960
Just my imagination?

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.180
It's been a while, Kudou Shinichi.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.100
No...

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.270
Isn't it "Edogawa Conan" now?

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:31.110
I'm surprised you're still alive, and as a kid.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.860
Really...

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.490
Hell of a surprise, eh, Partner?

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.030
How...

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.450
How did they discover my identity!?

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.530
Conan-kun?

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.580
Conan-kun, what's going on?

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:43.870
I heard some loud noises down there.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.210
Conan-kun?

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.460
Keep your eyes peeled.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:58.180
Bear witness to the destiny of the
people you've become involved with.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:01:59.890
Conan-kun!

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.220
Everything all right?

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.060
Conan-kun?

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.560
Where are you?

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.770
I'm coming in.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:22.700
Conan-kun?

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.120
RAN!

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.180
Shit...

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.520
What a nightmare...

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.370
I'm high school detective, Kudou Shinichi.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.750
While visiting an amusement park with my 
childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran...

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.470
I witnessed a man in black in the
midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.090
While caught up in watching the deal...

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.890
I failed to notice his partner coming up behind me.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.890
Those men forced me to swallow poison...

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.020
And when I came to...

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.310
My body had shrunk.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.900
If those guys found out that Kudou Shinichi was still alive...

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.860
They would come after me again...

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.610
And put those around me at risk.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.780
At Professor Agasa's suggestion,
I decided to conceal my true identity.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.790
When Ran asked for my name, in that instant...

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.950
I became Edogawa Conan.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.580
In order to obtain information on those guys...

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.880
I went to live with Ran, whose father is a private detective.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.800
Enshrouded in mystery, they are the Black Organization.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.470
Gin...

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:09.680
Vodka...

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:10.890
Vermouth...

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.350
Chianti...

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:12.770
Korn...

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.520
And Sherry.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.230
Her real name is Miyano Shiho.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.940
Her parents, who died when she was young...

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.820
Were scientists who worked for the Black Organization.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.860
Under the codename Sherry...

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.490
She, too, worked for the organization, and
developed the aforementioned drug...

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.080
Apotoxin-4869.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.040
However...

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.500
When her only older sister...

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.630
Miyano Akemi, was killed by the Organization, she revolted.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.800
She took the drug with the intention of taking her own life...

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.470
But instead, her body shrank as well.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.060
As such...

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.270
She changed her name to Haibara Ai.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.360
While evading the Organization...

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.650
She began living the life of a first grader, just as I had.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.360
Meanwhile...

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.820
I clashed with Vermouth, and came away with a vital clue.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:08.990
I wouldn't do that.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.450
If you attempt to unplug this device...

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.700
A signal will be sent out to my partner.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.170
With your boss's...

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.330
E-mail address.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.630
"Seven Children"!?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.130
Yeah.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.340
When you dial the boss's address, that's what you hear.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.010
The melody of that song, Seven Children.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.850
Don't tell me you're going to mail that address...

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.600
Idiot.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.760
Why would I do that?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:38.270
Well, I'll send a mail after Detective Takagi 
looks into the person behind this for me.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.980
He'll be killed...

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:40.980
Detective Takagi.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.150
It'll happen the very moment he reaches that person.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.910
And their next target...

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.120
Will be the one who provided him the mail address...

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.620
Which would be you, Kudou-kun.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.580
If you understand, just let it go and forget all about this.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.040
Because that e-mail address...

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:03.130
Is something that should never be opened: Pandora's Box.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.760
Even though I've become smaller, my mind remains the same...

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.600
The unbeaten great detective...

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.970
There's always only one truth!

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.860
Beika Forest

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.860
 Oh, there you are.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:28.240
I found one!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:28.780
A beetle.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.320
All right!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.330
So those beetles do like to gather at high places!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.280
All right!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.990
I'll climb up too!

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.700
That's impossible, Genta-kun.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.250
I think you'd better not.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:40.830
I agree.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.040
The only ones who can climb that high would be...

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.130
Either Edogawa-kun...

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.170
Or monkeys.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.220
Excuse me for being a monkey.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.640
I know, you can use the suspenders.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.430
Suspenders?

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:54.810
Oh...

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:57.100
These things you gave us back at your house?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.020
That's right―I've improved them a bit.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.690
With just a push of that button, they'Il extend up to 100 meters.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.570
Hold the button down, and the belt will elongate.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.990
Once you release it, the belt will immediately retract.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:17.740
My bad...

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.120
Jeez, be more careful.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.210
I found a beetle!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.170
That's great, Genta-kun.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.510
A rhinoceros beetle!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:31.380
It stopped!

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:33.840
There's two of them!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:35.930
A male and female!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:37.310
Huh?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.730
This female beetle...

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.980
Her wings have been taped.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:42.770
Look.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.350
It's true!

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.190
How mean!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.730
There are some words on it.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.990
Let's see...

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.820
Oh, it says "open".

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:54.780
This kind of tape is found on bento boxes 
that they sell in convenience stores.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.280
I saw it on that fried chicken bento I bought yesterday...

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:58.830
Fried chicken?

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.000
You've been secretly splurging again, haven't you?

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:06.040
Let me see, I'll get those off.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:06.380
Here.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.130
Who did this?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.510
What an awful prank.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.670
But, since there's a male and female here...

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.760
Could it be...

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.180
They're actually lover?

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.180
Then, Ayumi will name them!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.600
Let's see...

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.310
The boy will be called Hikoboshi!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.850
And the girl will be Orihime!

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:31.860
Hikoboshi symbolizes the star Altair, while Orihime is the star Vega. In mythology, the two 
represent a pair of lovers who can only meet on Tanabata (a star festival held in summer).

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.310
﻿That's great!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.440
﻿Now that you mention it, Tanabata is coming up.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.070
﻿Speaking of Tanabata...

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.030
﻿All right, got it off.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.900
﻿Time for the quiz you've been waiting for!

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:35.570
﻿No one's been waiting for that.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.330
﻿One year, on the night of Tanabata...

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.450
﻿It rained heavily, making it impossible for
﻿Orihime and Hikoboshi to meet with one another.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.670
﻿Troubled, those two thought hard...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.090
﻿And came up with a day called
﻿"The Day to Spend with Your Lover".

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.500
The Day to Spend with Your Lover
(Koibito to Tomo ni Sugosu Hi)

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:52.800
﻿Shortened, that would be "Lovers' Day",
﻿and so they met on that day instead.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:52.800
Lovers' Day
(Koi Tomo no Hi)

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.680
﻿Now, which of the following is that day?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.220
﻿#1 : New Year's Day on January 1st.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.520
﻿#2 : Setsubun on Februari 2nd.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.520
Bean- 
Throwing Day

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.270
﻿#3 : Momo-No-Sekku on March 3rd.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.270
Girl's Day

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.400
﻿#4 : Tango-No-Sekku on May 5th.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.400
Boy's Day

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:14.990
﻿I know!

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.950
﻿It's number three, Momo-No-Sekku, right?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.910
﻿Because Odairi-sama and Ohina-sama
﻿are lovers in the girl's doll set!

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.040
﻿Nope.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.910
﻿It's number four, Tango-No-Sekku.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.620
﻿Lovers like to dance to the passionate music of tango!

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.380
﻿I pick number one!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.380
﻿On New Year's Day, you can eat mochi dishes with your lover!

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.630
﻿You guys came up with a lot of ideas.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.630
﻿Professor!

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:38.260
﻿What's the answer?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.760
﻿It's number four, May 5th.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.140
﻿But my reasoning is...

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.060
May 5th, Boy's Day, is read "Kodomo no Hi."

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.730
﻿Kodomo no Hi

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.730
﻿Children's Day

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.060
If you separate the kanji for Kodomo no Hi...

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.940
﻿Ko  i  tomo  no  Hi

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.940
﻿Child "I" Together Day

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.070
You get "Ko-i-tomo-no-hi."

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.030
﻿Lovers' Day

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.030
﻿Koi, tomo no Hi

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.490
﻿I see...

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.490
﻿That's why you bothered to mention it was shortened
﻿from "The Day to Spend with Your Lover," right?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.290
﻿Lovers' Day," huh?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.420
﻿I hope that Hikoboshi-san and
﻿Orihime-san can be together forever!

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.750
﻿But still...

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:15.210
﻿Do you really think it's suitable to name
﻿two beetles Hikoboshi and Orihime?

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.010
﻿Is that so?

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.300
I think it's p﻿erfectly suitable.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:23.510
Orihime

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.220
﻿Orihime in English is Vega.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:26.180
Vega is part of the constellation Lyra.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:26.180
﻿The tape on the female beetle forms the
letter V, which is the initial of Vega, isn't it?

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:27.890
﻿True!

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:28.640
﻿It is suitable, huh?

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.860
﻿Well done, Haibara-san!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.780
﻿Say...

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.110
﻿How do I get down?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:48.500
﻿Damn...

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.210
﻿What's going on?

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:54.340
Stop!

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.050
﻿Stop!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.130
﻿Shit!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.770
Hey, you!

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:13.230
Are you all right?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.110
﻿Call an ambulance!

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:15.480
﻿Yes!

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.190
﻿Tanabata... Kyo...

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.120
﻿Hey, hang in there!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.370
﻿An ambulance is on the way!

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:26.580
﻿Hey!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.490
﻿Hey, you!

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:28.330
﻿Hang in there!

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:32.710
﻿Hear me?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.790
﻿I'm making an exception by bringing you here.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.750
﻿You have to behave yourself and wait out here.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.970
﻿Dad, your necktie is crooked.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:44.800
﻿Mouri-san!

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:47.930
﻿Thanks for coming so early in the morning.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.100
﻿Good morning, Ran-chan.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.680
﻿Conan-kun.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.310
﻿Good morning.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.110
﻿So this is a wide-scale serial murder case?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.360
﻿Right.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:59.940
﻿Our crime scene was at a turnpike in
﻿Odawara City, the day before yesterday.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.900
﻿We also discovered a mahjong tile there.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.450
﻿We already have several cases that
﻿include a mahjong tile discovery...

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:09.490
﻿Namely in Tokyo, Kanagawa, Shizuoka, and Nagano.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.620
﻿That brings the total number of prefectures involved to five.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.120
I see.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.460
﻿At any rate...

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.000
﻿Let's go over the remaining details in the conference.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:16.380
﻿Yeah.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:20.460
Please.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.800
﻿Isn't that Mouri-san!?

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:25.720
﻿Long time no see!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.680
﻿Your voice is as loud as ever, Yokomizo...

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:33.350
Yokomizo Juugo
Kanagawa Prefecture Police

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:33.350
Yokomizo Sango
Shizuoka Prefecture Police

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.480
I'm Sango.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.390
And this is my brother, Juugo.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.230
﻿I know that.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.100
﻿I've met him many times now.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.070
﻿Sango Juugo?

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.070
﻿3 (san) x 5 (go) = 15 (juugo)


00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.240
﻿And, who's this lady with you?

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.200
﻿Oh, pardon me.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.830
﻿This is an Inspector Ogino with the Saitama police.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:54.750
Ogino Ayami
Saitama Prefecture Police

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.290
I'm Ogino Ayami.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.790
I've heard much about you.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:59.460
﻿My, to think there's such a beautiful
﻿inspector working with the Saitama police!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:03.010
﻿When I worked in Saitama, she was my junior in terms of seniority.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.180
﻿Why the Saitama police?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:09.930
The victim who was killed in Tokyo
 ﻿was from Tokorozawa, Saitama.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.810
﻿That's why I was called to this conference.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:12.600
﻿And you, Mouri-san!

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.480
﻿Why are you here?

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:18.900
﻿He was invited to serve as a special advisor
﻿as per Superintendent Matsumoto's request.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.900
﻿To think we have to call upon a private detective for aid...

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.570
﻿Such a shame.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.690
﻿Agreed.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.570
You're...

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.660
Yamato Kansuke
Nagano Prefecture Police

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.160
Inspector Yamato Kansuke from Nagano police.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.200
And you're...

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.870
That quack detective with Gunma police!

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.870
That's mean, Mouri-san.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:38.540
Yamamura Misao
Gunma Prefecture Police

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.420
I do have a proper name, Yamamura Misao, you know?

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:39.790
Look!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:43.920
﻿But, didn't the incident happen in Nagano?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.340
﻿Why bring someone in from Gunma?

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:50.680
﻿Because the crime scene lies on the border
﻿of Nagano and Gunma, seeing as how...

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:55.560
﻿The victim's body from the knees down were in Gunma Prefecture!

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:56.020
﻿Right here!

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.730
﻿I already know your name.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.820
﻿Inspector!?

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.320
﻿You were promoted to inspector?

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.030
﻿Oh, you've noticed?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.660
﻿Thanks to everyone's assistance. I've been
﻿honorably promoted to the rank of inspector!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.330
﻿So, you're an inspector...

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.290
﻿Is Gunma really gonna make it?

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.170
﻿Say...

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.590
﻿Did the boy with glasses not come?

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.300
﻿Boy with glasses?

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.050
﻿You mean Conan?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:28.970
﻿Right, right!

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.430
﻿Edogawa Conan-kun!

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.470
﻿When he's around, cases always seem to get solved somehow!

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.220
﻿Come to think of it, that's happened to me as well.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.270
﻿It's happened to me also!

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.150
﻿You guys too?

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.230
﻿Actually, it's also happened to us.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.360
And then...

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:48.950
﻿You'd lose consciousness, and next thing
﻿you knew, the case would, be solved, right?

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.030
﻿Oops!

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.070
﻿Lose consciousness?

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:52.950
﻿Really?

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.990
﻿I don't think so.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:55.990
﻿Nah, nah, nah.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:57.660
﻿Just me?

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:59.830
﻿Yeah, you were the only one...

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.830
﻿﻿The only officer I tranquilized.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.090
﻿How weird...

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.130
﻿I'd like to commence the conference now.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.010
﻿Excuse us!

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.300
﻿Mouri-san!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.140
﻿Hey, Mouri-san!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:17.060
﻿Who is he?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.770
﻿That guy who looks so diabolical.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:22.560
Matsumoto Kiyonaga
Police Headquarters Superintendent

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.390
Idiot!

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.600
That's Superintendent Matsumoto Kiyonaga!

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:24.860
﻿With that face?

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.230
﻿If you keep that up, you're gonna get a beating!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.450
For starters...

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.870
﻿The common factor between the
﻿previous five cases but not the sixth...

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.620
﻿Was that all of the victims were
 ﻿stabbed to death with a large knife.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.660
﻿And judging-from the puncture wounds...

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.630
The killer raised their right arm and ﻿then plunged the knife downward.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:45.420
﻿Also...

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.880
﻿The victims in each of the five cases were
﻿attacked with a stun gun, kidnapped...

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:52.970
﻿And killed and left at the primary crime scenes.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:57.390
﻿Now, one question surfaces.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.470
﻿Why did our suspect, after disabling the victims...

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.600
﻿Take all of the extra time to relocate them...

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.020
﻿And only then proceed to kill?

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.190
﻿Next, on the bodies in all six cases...

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.650
﻿We found mahjong tiles with red circles on the front...

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:13.490
﻿And alphabet letters with black vertical
﻿lines through them on the back.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:17.200
﻿Tihese appear to be messages left by our killer.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.870
﻿About the red circles...

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:26.580
On the 7-Pin tiles, only the top-right and bottom- ﻿left four bottom circles are left unmarked.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.710
﻿The alphabet letters look like two A's, E, H, Z...

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.680
﻿Along with an upside-down L.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:38.300
﻿Also, among the accessories often carried by the six victims...

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:41.390
﻿One of each item was taken away.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:42.680
﻿A pendant...

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:43.560
﻿A small pouch...

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.440
﻿A keepsake...

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.360
﻿A motorcycle key holder, a make-up kit...

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.730
﻿And then a doll.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.990
﻿Could they have merely been dropped while
﻿they-were being kidnapped by the suspect?

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:57.320
﻿No, when it comes to only one of each item missing.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.450
﻿It's natural for us to assume they were taken by the suspect.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.410
﻿Our main question should be what
﻿the messages are supposed to mean.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.420
﻿There is one other message.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:11.800
﻿Left by our sixth victim, Ryuuzaki-san
﻿were the words: "Tanabata... Kyo."

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.670
﻿That was his dying message.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:19.220
﻿Ryuuzaki-san was probably at the rest house in
﻿Mount Daikan when his brake oil was leaked out...

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.140
﻿Which must also be where he saw his eventual murderer.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:23.560
﻿Everyone...

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.520
﻿Aren't you thinking a little too hard about this?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:32.030
﻿The mahjong tiles represent the game of mahjong itself.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:33.900
﻿The motive is simple...

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.610
﻿It's a dispute gone bad over mahjong.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.620
﻿The 1-Pin and 7-Pin tiles left by the suspect...

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:41.830
﻿Were meant to represent eight people playing Mahjong.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:46.660
﻿As for the 7-Pin tiles, only two circles remain unmarked in red.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.500
﻿One of them represents the suspect.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.590
﻿While the other...

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.050
﻿Represents the final victim.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.670
﻿You mean, the crime is still ongoing?

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.760
﻿Yes, I'm afraid so.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.300
﻿But...

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.680
﻿If it were meant to represent eight people...

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.640
﻿Wouldn't it be better to leave 8-Pin tiles?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.480
﻿There's actually one further meaning to the 1 and 7-Pin tiles.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:12.320
﻿The suspect was waiting for those
﻿two tiles in order to claim victory.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.320
﻿And with those, the suspect could
﻿have make an epic comeback!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.650
﻿I see!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.030
﻿Another player must've then won with a cheap combo!

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.870
﻿And that's when the suspect went crazy, right?

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:24.990
﻿Exactly!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:30.460
I'﻿m afraid all of his fellow players were
﻿engaging in this narrow-minded style of play!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.840
﻿The suspect couldn't take this lightly.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:37.590
﻿And that's the motive for you.

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.050
﻿Uhm...

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.300
﻿What do the alphabet letters mean, then?

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:44.060
﻿Why did the suspect take the extra time to
﻿transport the victims elsewhere for his kills?

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:45.680
﻿Also...

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.980
﻿Regarding Ryuuzaki-san's dying message, what does it...

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.060
A﻿bout that...

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:53.060
W﻿ell, as for that...

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.110
﻿As for that...

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.490
﻿We'll find out as we go.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:00.360
﻿Superintendent.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:07.660
﻿Let's ponder the significance of
﻿those six locations to the suspect.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:13.630
Should there be any significance, it could
﻿very well lead us right to our killer.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.170
﻿As for the six victims...

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:20.800
﻿They're-bound to be related to the suspect somehow. ﻿

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:24.300
﻿Discovering the common factor among these six...

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.600
﻿Will be the fastest way to get to the killer.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.980
﻿It's still possible that the connecting link lies in
﻿a game of mahjong, as Mouri-kun suggested.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:36.520
﻿Also, the alphabet letters and black
﻿lines on the back of the mahjong tiles...

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:41.070
﻿Along with the dying message "Tanabata...
﻿Kyo," are problems you need to unravel.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.370
﻿Listen up, everyone.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.540
﻿It's extremely likely our suspect will commit another crime.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.210
﻿We have to bet our pride as police and put a stop to this.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.210
﻿At times like this, we must put aside our
﻿territorial imperatives and rivalries...

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.710
And promote the free exchange
 ﻿of information with one another...

00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:00.840
﻿In order to capture our suspect as soon as possible.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.970
﻿I urge you to do your best in your investigations.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:04.800
﻿Yes, sir!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.230
﻿Bathroom, bathroom!

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:11.850
﻿Can't hold it!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.480
﻿Looks like it's over, the meeting.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:15.610
﻿Looks like it.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.690
﻿Officer Matsumoto!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.110
﻿Long time no see.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.780
﻿Is Sayuri-sensei doing well?

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.950
Ah, you're Mouri's...

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.660
﻿My daughter's doing just fine.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.410
Well, Mouri...

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:33.160
﻿I'm counting on you.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.130
﻿Your humble Mouri Kogorou...

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:40.300
﻿Now vows to meet your expectations by doing his very best!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.340
﻿Thank you for your work!

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.140
﻿Oh?

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.980
﻿Detective Chiba, did you lose a little weight?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.140
﻿Oh, you noticed?

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.400
﻿I'm on a diet now.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.320
﻿It's popular on that morning TV program, you know?

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.440
﻿Speaking of weight...

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:01.940
﻿Shiratori...

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.650
﻿Haven't you gained some by comparison?

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.570
﻿Let's not joke around, Mouri-san.

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.580
﻿I go to the gym twice a week, you know.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.040
How unusual.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.830
﻿Big bro's drinking black coffee?

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:17.250
﻿Yeah.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.420
Th﻿e doctor put a limit on my sugar intake.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.670
﻿And speaking of which, didn't you hate sweet stuff?

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.550
﻿Three murder cases in a row on my desk.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.590
﻿I can't function without glucose!

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.100
﻿Uhm, Inspector Yokomizo...

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:32.600
Oh, no...

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.140
﻿I mean the elder of you.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.020
﻿Right.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:35.940
﻿Say...

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:39.110
﻿Is that the boy you've been talking about, Edogawa Conan-kun?

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:39.730
﻿Yeah!

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:42.980
﻿Because he's always listening to Mouri-san's deductions...

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.950
﻿Sometimes, he'll say things that turn out to be surprising hints.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:49.120
﻿And, he often notices little interesting things.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.280
﻿Even things we pros may overlook.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.750
﻿Is that so?

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.460
﻿Oh, crow~

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.000
Why do you cry~

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:09.220
﻿'Cause in the mountain, the crow~

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:09.970
﻿Hey!

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.510
﻿Detective Yamamura, that song...

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:16.730
﻿I see you haven't taken notice yet, but I'm actually...

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:20.520
﻿Why were you just singing that song?

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:21.400
﻿"Inspector" Yamamura.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:23.110
"Why," you ask?

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:25.690
﻿Well, I just heard it outside the bathroom.

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.820
﻿It sounded like push-button dial tones.

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:29.570
﻿When I left the bathroom...

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:32.240
I saw an officer with glasses dialing on his cellphone and...

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:34.540
﻿Wait, Conan-kun...

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:35.700
﻿Don't tell me...

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:37.410
﻿﻿Don't tell me, those guys...

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:38.790
﻿﻿Don't tell me...

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:44.130
﻿There!

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:48.590
Hey, Conan-kun?

00:22:48.590 --> 00:22:49.550
﻿Something wrong?

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:50.720
﻿Damn!

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:51.930
﻿Going to the bathroom!

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:52.550
﻿Conan-kun?

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:56.140
﻿But there's a bathroom right behind me...

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:08.190
﻿﻿That was a Porsche 356A...

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:09.650
﻿﻿Gin's car!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:11.360
﻿﻿Why?

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.240
﻿﻿Why were they in the conference?

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:16.490
﻿﻿Exactly what is their objective?

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:20.540
﻿What now?

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:22.380
﻿They infiltrated the police conference?

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:24.210
﻿You're too loud!

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.970
﻿I hope Haibara didn't hear that.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:33.260
﻿I think she's in the lab downstairs.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:35.850
﻿Most likely...

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:37.720
﻿The disguised officer would've been Vermouth.

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.560
﻿While waiting for the elevator to arrive...

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:43.230
﻿She must have mailed her boss about the meeting.

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:44.860
﻿I see.

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:47.360
﻿And that's what Detective Yamamura overheard...

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:52.070
﻿The push-button tones that sounded like Seven
﻿Children as she input her boss's address.

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:55.410
﻿But why...

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:56.530
My, my...

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:59.160
﻿And here I was wondering what it
﻿was you two were whispering about.

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:00.330
﻿Haibara!

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:01.790
﻿And?

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:03.370
﻿Why did you think it was Vermouth?

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:05.960
﻿The push-button tones alone won't...

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.550
﻿Because Gin's Porsche was there too.

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:12.930
The risk would be too high for them to ﻿infiltrate the police without a disguise.

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:17.890
﻿When it comes to disguises, Vermouth does it best.

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:20.020
﻿At any rate...

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:26.400
It's now safe to assume that these cases
 ﻿somehow concern the Black Organization.

00:24:27.020 --> 00:24:29.690
﻿And I'd like to investigate these cases as well.

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:31.690
﻿Think you can lend me a hand?

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:34.160
I don't mind, but...

00:24:35.780 --> 00:24:37.660
﻿Even if I did tell you to stop...

00:24:37.660 --> 00:24:39.160
﻿You wouId never give up, would you?

00:24:39.830 --> 00:24:41.660
﻿But, you need to be on high alert.

00:24:42.580 --> 00:24:44.250
﻿I'm sure you're already aware, but...

00:24:44.250 --> 00:24:46.040
﻿If your identity were to be exposed to them...

00:24:46.750 --> 00:24:47.790
﻿Yeah.

00:24:47.790 --> 00:24:48.630
﻿I know.

