﻿No doubt about that.

00:58:19.970 --> 00:58:22.600
﻿When Jinno-san got on, the buzzer sounded.

00:58:22.600 --> 00:58:24.680
﻿That's why he wanted someone out.

00:58:25.640 --> 00:58:28.150
﻿The scapegoat turned out to be Nanako-san!

00:58:29.060 --> 00:58:31.770
﻿The other six either pretended not to notice or...

00:58:31.770 --> 00:58:36.490
﻿Feared that they, themselves, would be forced
﻿out, and decided to cooperate with Jinno-san.

00:58:37.530 --> 00:58:40.570
﻿After being unable to ride the elevator, Nanako-san...

00:58:40.570 --> 00:58:42.160
﻿Died after being unable to escape.

00:58:44.290 --> 00:58:44.910
﻿﻿What's wrong?

00:58:44.910 --> 00:58:46.330
﻿﻿There a problem with my deduction?

00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:47.830
﻿No...

00:58:47.830 --> 00:58:50.920
﻿It's just that I still don't understand
﻿what the letters on the tiles mean.

00:58:51.420 --> 00:58:52.500
﻿Yeah.

00:58:52.500 --> 00:58:56.880
It ﻿is strange that there was a triangle
﻿instead of a letter on the seventh tile.

00:58:58.470 --> 00:59:01.550
﻿Well, if the last circle really does represent Nanako-san...

00:59:01.550 --> 00:59:03.260
﻿﻿There shouldn't be any more murders.

00:59:03.850 --> 00:59:04.930
﻿I hope so.

00:59:05.850 --> 00:59:06.770
﻿At any rate...

00:59:06.770 --> 00:59:08.020
﻿I'll try to locate Mizutani-san.

00:59:09.270 --> 00:59:10.900
﻿Thank you, Hattori.

00:59:11.690 --> 00:59:12.190
﻿For real.

00:59:12.730 --> 00:59:13.400
﻿Kudou...

00:59:15.030 --> 00:59:15.820
﻿Tell you what!

00:59:15.820 --> 00:59:18.780
﻿I found an awesome restaurant
﻿that serves Okonomiyaki dishes.

00:59:18.780 --> 00:59:21.030
﻿We'll pay it a visit the next time you come over.

00:59:24.370 --> 00:59:25.410
﻿You have to come.

00:59:26.200 --> 00:59:27.450
﻿I'll be waiting.

00:59:30.120 --> 00:59:32.130
﻿Yeah, I know.

00:59:32.130 --> 00:59:32.710
﻿Later.

00:59:37.460 --> 00:59:38.420
﻿Kudou...

00:59:39.590 --> 00:59:40.510
﻿You have to.

00:59:43.970 --> 00:59:44.810
﻿What?

00:59:44.810 --> 00:59:46.600
﻿On July 7th two years ago?

00:59:47.020 --> 00:59:50.100
﻿All victims were in Kyoto on that day?

00:59:50.480 --> 00:59:51.270
﻿Yeah.

00:59:51.270 --> 00:59:53.310
﻿We've confirmed it through our investigations.

00:59:53.980 --> 00:59:55.110
﻿That means..

00:59:55.110 --> 00:59:58.280
﻿The "Tanabata... Kyo” our witness heard...

00:59:58.280 --> 01:00:01.610
﻿Appears to really be "Tanabata Kyoto."

01:00:01.610 --> 01:00:02.360
﻿As for that day...

01:00:02.990 --> 01:00:06.450
﻿I have people looking into exactly
﻿what happened in Kyoto then.

01:00:06.490 --> 01:00:07.200
Th﻿e question is...

01:00:07.910 --> 01:00:11.330
﻿What do these messages the culprit has left
﻿us on the mahjong tiles actually mean?

01:00:11.330 --> 01:00:16.050
﻿Only the bottom-left circle hasn't been marked red...

01:00:16.050 --> 01:00:19.590
﻿Which means it's probable there will be another murder.

01:00:19.590 --> 01:00:20.130
﻿And...

01:00:20.840 --> 01:00:24.220
It looks like it's no coincidence that today is July 7th as well.

01:00:24.220 --> 01:00:25.050
﻿Then...

01:00:25.050 --> 01:00:26.600
﻿Then, the last person will die today?

01:00:27.350 --> 01:00:29.180
﻿Where and who?

01:00:31.100 --> 01:00:32.350
﻿﻿Could it be that...

01:00:32.350 --> 01:00:33.310
﻿﻿Someone here...

01:00:41.700 --> 01:00:42.820
﻿I've got it!

01:00:43.410 --> 01:00:48.200
﻿The seven locations represent the shape of a certain animal!

01:00:48.200 --> 01:00:49.540
﻿A certain animal?

01:00:50.290 --> 01:00:51.790
Here, look.

01:00:52.120 --> 01:00:56.380
﻿If we connect the lines between all of the crime scenes...

01:00:59.340 --> 01:01:01.260
﻿Do you get it now?

01:01:04.130 --> 01:01:05.930
﻿This long line is the neck.

01:01:05.930 --> 01:01:07.220
﻿And here's the chest.

01:01:07.220 --> 01:01:08.100
﻿The front leg.

01:01:08.100 --> 01:01:08.930
﻿The back.

01:01:08.930 --> 01:01:10.640
﻿And the hind leg.

01:01:10.640 --> 01:01:13.390
﻿So, instead of Nessie from Loch Ness...

01:01:13.690 --> 01:01:14.600
﻿It's Assie!

01:01:15.100 --> 01:01:17.190
﻿From Lake Ashino!

01:01:17.190 --> 01:01:18.270
﻿Quack, quack!

01:01:18.860 --> 01:01:20.110
﻿Assie?

01:01:21.490 --> 01:01:23.360
﻿Is there even such a thing?

01:01:23.360 --> 01:01:25.610
﻿Nah, never heard of it.

01:01:26.030 --> 01:01:28.410
﻿I don't get it at all.

01:01:28.780 --> 01:01:30.580
﻿Well then...

01:01:30.580 --> 01:01:31.870
﻿How about this?

01:01:33.210 --> 01:01:34.830
﻿If you say so...

01:01:35.290 --> 01:01:36.330
﻿I can see it!

01:01:36.330 --> 01:01:37.130
﻿It's Assie!

01:01:38.000 --> 01:01:39.670
﻿But, why Assie?

01:01:40.130 --> 01:01:41.670
﻿It could be Lake Yamanaka's Yassie...

01:01:41.960 --> 01:01:44.170
﻿Pay attention to the shape of the lake.

01:01:44.430 --> 01:01:46.140
﻿Lake Yamanaka is shaped like a whale.

01:01:46.510 --> 01:01:47.970
﻿What about Lake Ashino?

01:01:49.930 --> 01:01:51.560
﻿I get it, Mouri-san!

01:01:52.020 --> 01:01:55.390
﻿The next crime scene will be at Assie's nose!

01:01:56.600 --> 01:01:58.650
﻿Amateur, Inspector Yokomizo!

01:01:58.650 --> 01:02:00.900
﻿They wanted us to think that...

01:02:01.190 --> 01:02:02.360
﻿But, in fact, it's really here!

01:02:02.570 --> 01:02:03.320
﻿I see!

01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:04.280
﻿It's the eye!

01:02:04.280 --> 01:02:05.490
﻿It's in Gunma Prefecture's Annaka City!

01:02:06.160 --> 01:02:08.120
﻿I know Annaka City well!

01:02:08.700 --> 01:02:09.950
﻿I'll head over there too!

01:02:09.950 --> 01:02:10.580
﻿Lead us!

01:02:10.950 --> 01:02:11.660
﻿Yes!

01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:12.790
﻿I'll go too!

01:02:15.250 --> 01:02:16.580
﻿What're you...

01:02:16.580 --> 01:02:17.580
﻿Stop it.

01:02:17.580 --> 01:02:20.000
﻿But with only the two of them against a vicious killer...

01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:21.380
﻿Two's enough.

01:02:27.220 --> 01:02:27.930
﻿That was fun!

01:02:27.930 --> 01:02:28.760
﻿Yep.

01:02:28.760 --> 01:02:30.970
﻿Would've been nice if Conan-kun had come.

01:02:30.970 --> 01:02:33.850
﻿Say, don't you think Conan's been weird lately?

01:02:34.350 --> 01:02:36.890
﻿He went home alone again today.

01:02:36.890 --> 01:02:39.480
﻿I bet his cold hasn't gone away yet.

01:02:39.480 --> 01:02:41.900
﻿Remember, he even took two days off from school?

01:02:42.940 --> 01:02:43.610
﻿It's here!

01:02:53.870 --> 01:02:54.870
﻿It's a rhinoceros beetle!

01:02:55.500 --> 01:02:57.790
﻿This bus must have come from Beika Forest.

01:02:58.210 --> 01:02:59.330
﻿I see!

01:02:59.330 --> 01:03:01.790
The beetle flew onto that man's
 ﻿shoulder while in the forest.

01:03:01.790 --> 01:03:03.550
﻿And got on with him!

01:03:05.050 --> 01:03:06.340
﻿Convenience store tape!

01:03:06.550 --> 01:03:08.090
﻿Again?

01:03:08.090 --> 01:03:10.640
﻿Looks like they're playing pranks on other beetles too.

01:03:10.640 --> 01:03:11.640
﻿How sad.

01:03:12.180 --> 01:03:13.140
﻿No use.

01:03:13.140 --> 01:03:14.930
﻿The tape's on there really tight.

01:03:14.930 --> 01:03:17.680
Let's ask the professor to peel it off again.

01:03:17.680 --> 01:03:20.020
﻿And to treat us to something!

01:03:49.260 --> 01:03:50.470
﻿Kazuki-san...

01:03:50.470 --> 01:03:53.970
﻿There was only one anonymous bouquet this time.

01:03:53.970 --> 01:03:54.850
﻿Looks that way.

01:03:58.270 --> 01:03:59.180
﻿Hello.

01:04:01.850 --> 01:04:03.980
﻿You're Detective-Mouri's assistant?

01:04:03.980 --> 01:04:04.650
Is that true?

01:04:06.480 --> 01:04:10.990
﻿And, I'm searching for Mizutani-san
﻿as part of an investigation, but...

01:04:10.990 --> 01:04:12.700
﻿It seems he didn't come to
﻿the memorial service, huh?

01:04:13.030 --> 01:04:13.990
﻿Yeah.

01:04:13.990 --> 01:04:15.780
﻿He came here at early dawn...

01:04:15.780 --> 01:04:17.200
﻿And hurriedly left a bouquet before leaving.

01:04:18.160 --> 01:04:19.410
﻿Just left a bouquet?

01:04:19.410 --> 01:04:19.960
﻿Yeah.

01:04:20.750 --> 01:04:25.920
﻿My parents still cannot forgive him
﻿for running away with my sister.

01:04:27.130 --> 01:04:27.670
﻿That's why...

01:04:28.090 --> 01:04:28.630
﻿Then...

01:04:28.630 --> 01:04:31.300
﻿The one she said was left anonymously...

01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:32.130
﻿Was that Mizutani-san?

01:04:33.050 --> 01:04:34.930
﻿She mentioned it was the "only" one today...

01:04:34.930 --> 01:04:37.180
﻿Which means there were other anonymous ones before, right?

01:04:37.180 --> 01:04:38.970
﻿Yeah, other than his.

01:04:39.470 --> 01:04:40.310
﻿When?

01:04:40.310 --> 01:04:41.600
﻿And do you know from where?

01:04:42.270 --> 01:04:42.980
﻿I do.

01:04:43.980 --> 01:04:45.520
Let's see...

01:04:45.520 --> 01:04:48.030
﻿Four on the day of the funeral two years ago...

01:04:48.030 --> 01:04:49.570
﻿From Matsumoto City, Kawasaki...

01:04:49.900 --> 01:04:51.820
﻿Numazu, and Kamakura.

01:04:52.530 --> 01:04:54.280
﻿Three on the memorial service day last year...

01:04:54.660 --> 01:04:57.740
﻿That time from Tokorozawa, Odawara, and Hachioji.

01:04:58.580 --> 01:05:01.000
﻿﻿All seven were from where the victims lived...

01:05:01.790 --> 01:05:04.000
﻿Actually, when I met Kousuke-kun this morning...

01:05:04.790 --> 01:05:06.380
﻿He said something strange.

01:05:07.000 --> 01:05:07.960
﻿Something strange?

01:05:08.710 --> 01:05:10.420
"﻿There were eight people I could not forgive."

01:05:11.380 --> 01:05:13.510
"﻿Now, only one remains."

01:05:17.890 --> 01:05:21.270
﻿This was doneby the same culprit.

01:05:22.020 --> 01:05:24.650
﻿The way they taped the V-shape is the same.

01:05:25.690 --> 01:05:26.810
﻿I see!

01:05:26.810 --> 01:05:28.770
﻿This could be someone's message.

01:05:29.480 --> 01:05:30.480
﻿Message?

01:05:30.900 --> 01:05:34.070
﻿Now, do you know what the message is?

01:05:39.200 --> 01:05:41.660
﻿The answer is "Help," an S.O.S.

01:05:43.120 --> 01:05:43.960
﻿Why?

01:05:45.710 --> 01:05:47.750
﻿This bug is known as a "beetle" in English.

01:05:48.380 --> 01:05:52.880
﻿My Volkswagen has a similar shape
﻿so it's also known as a Beetle.

01:05:53.550 --> 01:05:54.840
﻿Also...

01:05:54.840 --> 01:05:58.640
﻿After combining the word "beetle" with
﻿the musical term "beat," you get...

01:05:59.140 --> 01:06:01.430
﻿The name of the legendary band, The Beatles!

01:06:01.890 --> 01:06:03.890
﻿"Beatles," you say?

01:06:04.480 --> 01:06:08.900
﻿Their first album was titled, "Please Please Me."

01:06:09.230 --> 01:06:11.650
The second, "With the Beatles."

01:06:12.110 --> 01:06:14.780
﻿The third, "A Hard Day's Night."

01:06:18.240 --> 01:06:20.660
﻿And the fifth, is "Help!"

01:06:23.910 --> 01:06:24.710
﻿How's that?

01:06:24.710 --> 01:06:25.790
﻿See now?

01:06:26.160 --> 01:06:27.960
﻿What is "The Beatles"?

01:06:27.960 --> 01:06:29.960
﻿Sounds like a foreign band.

01:06:30.960 --> 01:06:32.920
﻿You guys don't know The Beatles?

01:06:33.130 --> 01:06:34.630
﻿Not at all.

01:06:34.920 --> 01:06:37.680
﻿I remember my sister listening to them occasionally.

01:06:38.720 --> 01:06:40.470
She loved the oldies.

01:06:41.640 --> 01:06:42.970
﻿"The oldies"?

01:06:46.310 --> 01:06:49.310
﻿I wish he had treated us to food instead of quizzes.

01:06:50.610 --> 01:06:55.190
"﻿Help!" means someone is asking for our assistance, right?

01:06:55.820 --> 01:06:56.530
I see.

01:07:02.240 --> 01:07:03.700
﻿I finally understand.

01:07:03.700 --> 01:07:05.450
﻿The meaning of "Tanabata Kyoto."

01:07:06.500 --> 01:07:08.290
﻿All seven victims checked in?

01:07:08.750 --> 01:07:13.130
﻿﻿The victim of the fire was a young girl named Honjou Nanako.

01:07:13.130 --> 01:07:16.090
﻿﻿And, her boyfriend by the name of Mizutani Kousuke...

01:07:16.090 --> 01:07:19.050
﻿﻿Came here to look into this case a year ago.

01:07:19.380 --> 01:07:20.640
Also...

01:07:20.640 --> 01:07:21.760
﻿Two hours ago...

01:07:21.760 --> 01:07:25.390
﻿That Hattori Heiji-kun came and inquired about the same thing.

01:07:25.970 --> 01:07:27.180
Yeah, that's right.

01:07:27.230 --> 01:07:29.100
﻿I have a bit of interest in the case.

01:07:29.560 --> 01:07:30.770
﻿Right, right, Inspector.

01:07:31.310 --> 01:07:32.860
﻿I'll share something juicy with you.

01:07:33.520 --> 01:07:36.110
﻿The mahjong tiles represent an elevator.

01:07:36.360 --> 01:07:37.440
﻿Elevator?

01:07:43.160 --> 01:07:45.990
﻿The number of guests staying on the
﻿hotel's sixth floor amounted to nine.

01:07:46.700 --> 01:07:50.920
﻿Not counting the deceased
﻿Nanako-san and Mizutani himself...

01:07:50.920 --> 01:07:52.750
﻿All other seven were killed.

01:07:53.840 --> 01:07:55.630
﻿Just who is this final person?

01:07:55.670 --> 01:07:56.550
﻿Oh, I know.

01:07:58.050 --> 01:08:00.090
﻿This is chouzu, isn't it?

01:08:00.090 --> 01:08:01.930
﻿Right, you know a lot!

01:08:02.300 --> 01:08:04.760
﻿But I don't know what to do with this dipper.

01:08:05.220 --> 01:08:06.430
﻿Is that so?

01:08:06.430 --> 01:08:07.720
﻿I'll teach you then.

01:08:07.720 --> 01:08:08.730
﻿All right.

01:08:18.570 --> 01:08:18.940
﻿What?

01:08:19.400 --> 01:08:21.030
﻿The location of the stars?

01:08:21.030 --> 01:08:21.320
﻿Yeah.

01:08:21.950 --> 01:08:23.450
﻿The seven crime scenes...

01:08:23.450 --> 01:08:27.790
﻿Represent locations relative to Polaris
﻿and the six stars in the Big Dipper.

01:08:27.790 --> 01:08:28.750
﻿Hold on.

01:08:36.420 --> 01:08:37.670
﻿It's true.

01:08:37.670 --> 01:08:39.130
﻿They're not just similar.

01:08:39.970 --> 01:08:43.590
﻿They align perfectly with the actual photo of the stars.

01:08:44.430 --> 01:08:46.560
﻿What a perfectionist, our killer.

01:08:47.010 --> 01:08:48.180
﻿Just the same...

01:08:48.180 --> 01:08:50.060
﻿The mahjong tiles and letters...

01:08:50.060 --> 01:08:53.060
﻿All represent Polaris and the Big Dipper.

01:08:54.480 --> 01:08:58.400
The 1-Pin and﻿ 7-Pins all indicate the
shape of Polaris and the Big Dipper.

01:08:59.190 --> 01:09:00.150
﻿And the letters...

01:08:59.690 --> 01:09:08.030
Polaris

01:08:59.690 --> 01:09:08.030
Dubhe

01:08:59.690 --> 01:09:08.030
Merak

