01:09:07.240 --> 01:09:08.540
As Greek letters.

01:09:09.120 --> 01:09:09.910
﻿So, Haibara?

01:09:10.620 --> 01:09:12.330
﻿The location of the remaining Big Dipper star...

01:09:12.330 --> 01:09:13.870
﻿Merak, right?

01:09:13.870 --> 01:09:14.960
﻿Right away.

01:09:14.960 --> 01:09:15.460
﻿Thanks.

01:09:16.290 --> 01:09:16.840
﻿There.

01:09:17.380 --> 01:09:19.420
﻿Shiba Park, in Minato Ward.

01:09:20.840 --> 01:09:25.640
The person who sent the "Help!" message
should be near that oak tree we visited before.

01:09:26.430 --> 01:09:27.890
﻿We need to rescue them!

01:09:27.890 --> 01:09:28.640
﻿Yeah!

01:09:28.640 --> 01:09:30.180
﻿Detective Boys...

01:09:30.180 --> 01:09:32.230
﻿Commence!

01:09:38.480 --> 01:09:40.820
﻿If this is about Mizutani-kun and Nanako-san...

01:09:40.820 --> 01:09:44.110
﻿A boy with glasses came and asked about
﻿the same thing a couple of hours ago.

01:09:45.030 --> 01:09:46.410
﻿Boy with glasses?

01:09:46.410 --> 01:09:47.320
﻿Yeah.

01:09:47.320 --> 01:09:48.910
﻿He said he was Detective Mouri's assistant.

01:09:51.040 --> 01:09:53.410
﻿And these were Mizutani-san's words, correct?

01:09:54.080 --> 01:09:56.330
"﻿There were eight people I could not forgive."

01:09:56.330 --> 01:09:58.290
﻿Now, only one remains.

01:09:58.290 --> 01:09:58.880
﻿Yeah.

01:09:59.420 --> 01:10:00.420
﻿What happened?

01:10:01.130 --> 01:10:02.170
﻿Did Mizutani-kun...

01:10:02.760 --> 01:10:04.510
﻿No, just asking.

01:10:04.510 --> 01:10:05.130
﻿What?

01:10:05.680 --> 01:10:08.600
﻿You mean our suspect plans to kill another?

01:10:08.970 --> 01:10:10.560
﻿﻿Yes, I'm afraid so.

01:10:10.560 --> 01:10:13.520
﻿﻿Also, Conan-kun came here earlier as well.

01:10:13.520 --> 01:10:15.060
﻿Conan-kun did?

01:10:16.440 --> 01:10:17.020
﻿Nah.

01:10:17.400 --> 01:10:20.650
﻿How could I ask him to do something like that?

01:10:20.650 --> 01:10:21.820
﻿That brat.

01:10:22.230 --> 01:10:23.820
﻿Then, who else could it be?

01:10:24.490 --> 01:10:26.150
﻿Could it be Kudou-kun?

01:10:26.150 --> 01:10:26.860
﻿Superintendent...

01:10:26.950 --> 01:10:29.240
﻿Would that not mean Mizutani Kousuke is the culprit?

01:10:29.240 --> 01:10:30.240
﻿Yeah.

01:10:30.240 --> 01:10:31.990
﻿I think that assumption is valid.

01:10:32.490 --> 01:10:34.540
﻿But who is this last person?

01:10:35.160 --> 01:10:37.250
﻿Where will the next crime scene be?

01:10:50.640 --> 01:10:51.470
﻿Nana...

01:10:53.140 --> 01:10:54.770
﻿﻿Kousuke!

01:10:57.230 --> 01:10:58.690
﻿﻿﻿Hey, can I try again?

01:10:59.350 --> 01:11:00.730
﻿﻿﻿I'm so excited.

01:11:01.400 --> 01:11:03.900
﻿﻿﻿This is my first trip with Kousuke!

01:11:04.230 --> 01:11:05.150
﻿﻿﻿Kousuke!

01:11:14.740 --> 01:11:15.500
﻿﻿﻿Nana! Nana!

01:11:15.500 --> 01:11:16.500
﻿﻿﻿Let me go!

01:11:16.500 --> 01:11:18.000
﻿﻿﻿Nana's in there!

01:11:18.000 --> 01:11:18.670
﻿﻿Nana!

01:11:18.710 --> 01:11:19.670
﻿﻿﻿Nana!

01:11:22.460 --> 01:11:23.210
﻿Nana...

01:11:28.300 --> 01:11:29.130
﻿Understood.

01:11:29.760 --> 01:11:32.720
﻿I'll go look for him as well.

01:11:32.720 --> 01:11:33.310
﻿Thanks.

01:11:33.760 --> 01:11:35.720
﻿Even Tsuburaya-kun hasn't gone home?

01:11:35.770 --> 01:11:36.430
﻿Yeah.

01:11:36.430 --> 01:11:39.520
﻿It's already 7:00; where could those three be?

01:11:40.100 --> 01:11:42.980
﻿I tried to get them on their Detective
﻿Badges, but they aren't answering.

01:11:44.440 --> 01:11:46.480
﻿Say, Professor, could those three have...

01:11:55.370 --> 01:11:56.490
﻿﻿Yes?

01:11:56.490 --> 01:11:57.290
﻿Sawamura-san?

01:11:59.040 --> 01:12:00.830
﻿Mizutani-kun and Nanako-san's hobby?

01:12:02.170 --> 01:12:04.500
﻿Could it have been star-gazing?

01:12:04.500 --> 01:12:05.000
﻿﻿That's right.

01:12:05.670 --> 01:12:09.380
﻿He said he chose to live here because
﻿of its proximity to the observatory.

01:12:09.380 --> 01:12:10.130
﻿﻿﻿As I thought.

01:12:10.470 --> 01:12:11.550
﻿Of all the stars...

01:12:11.550 --> 01:12:14.640
﻿They loved Polaris and the Big Dipper the most.

01:12:15.890 --> 01:12:17.930
﻿The beautiful shape of the Big Dipper...

01:12:18.640 --> 01:12:21.640
﻿And Polaris shining right above the north pole...

01:12:25.520 --> 01:12:30.610
﻿I think they strengthened their love by gazing at those stars.

01:12:32.200 --> 01:12:33.950
﻿Well, a kid like you...

01:12:34.370 --> 01:12:35.780
﻿﻿﻿You wouldn't understand.

01:12:35.780 --> 01:12:36.490
﻿Thanks.

01:12:38.120 --> 01:12:41.250
﻿﻿﻿The place here that's nearest the stars would be...

01:12:46.840 --> 01:12:47.880
﻿﻿﻿Good evening!

01:12:48.460 --> 01:12:53.090
﻿﻿﻿I'm currently at Touto Tower, where
﻿the Tanabata Fair is being held.

01:12:53.640 --> 01:12:57.510
﻿﻿﻿Unfortunately, even though it's cloudy,
 ﻿tonight is the last night of the fair.

01:12:58.220 --> 01:13:01.560
﻿﻿Visitors wearing beautiful
 ﻿yukatas are gathering all around.

01:13:01.980 --> 01:13:05.020
﻿﻿﻿Next is our weather forecast for tonight and tomorrow.

01:13:05.190 --> 01:13:06.860
﻿Wearing a yukata on a date, huh?

01:13:05.360 --> 01:13:09.150
There is a high chance of rain in the
Tokyo area around 10:00 tonight.

01:13:09.690 --> 01:13:11.360
﻿﻿﻿Thunderstorms are expected elsewhere.

01:13:14.860 --> 01:13:16.450
﻿Miss!

01:13:18.240 --> 01:13:19.240
﻿What is it, boy?

01:13:19.790 --> 01:13:21.540
﻿Can you watch this for me?

01:13:22.830 --> 01:13:23.870
﻿I can, but...

01:13:23.870 --> 01:13:24.670
﻿Are you alone?

01:13:25.210 --> 01:13:27.500
﻿When I went to the bathroom...

01:13:27.500 --> 01:13:30.340
﻿My daddy and brother left without me.

01:13:30.710 --> 01:13:32.090
﻿Meanies? aren't they?

01:13:39.180 --> 01:13:41.810
﻿Hitomi-chan, your yukata's beautiful!

01:13:41.810 --> 01:13:42.890
﻿Moeri-chan, yours is cute!

01:13:43.310 --> 01:13:45.980
﻿Hey, let's take a picture of us four!

01:13:45.980 --> 01:13:47.560
﻿Take a lot, a lot!

01:13:47.900 --> 01:13:49.320
﻿All right, cheese!

01:13:49.320 --> 01:13:50.400
﻿Cheese!

01:14:07.380 --> 01:14:09.540
﻿Have we been here before?

01:14:13.510 --> 01:14:14.510
﻿Did we take the wrong path?

01:14:15.590 --> 01:14:16.720
﻿Let's go home.

01:14:16.970 --> 01:14:17.840
﻿No way!

01:14:17.840 --> 01:14:19.970
﻿We must find this person ourselves!

01:14:19.970 --> 01:14:20.720
﻿That's right.

01:14:21.220 --> 01:14:24.930
﻿Don't you want to solve a case without Conan-kun for once?

01:14:25.850 --> 01:14:26.390
﻿I do!

01:14:27.020 --> 01:14:30.360
﻿But we can't seem to find that oak tree...

01:14:33.110 --> 01:14:34.070
﻿Ah, I know!

01:14:34.740 --> 01:14:37.110
﻿Let's ask this beetle to show us the way.

01:14:37.110 --> 01:14:41.160
﻿Beetles usually fly towards the tree with the same sap.

01:14:45.460 --> 01:14:46.460
﻿That way!

01:14:47.500 --> 01:14:48.710
﻿Do we have to run?

01:14:52.170 --> 01:14:54.590
﻿Through our investigation, we
﻿have identified the suspect...

01:14:54.590 --> 01:14:58.010
﻿And have determined that it's highly
﻿probable he will commit another murder.

01:14:58.130 --> 01:14:59.050
However...

01:14:59.050 --> 01:15:02.760
﻿We still do not know the whereabouts of the
 ﻿suspect nor the location of his next crime.

01:15:03.430 --> 01:15:05.230
﻿Any ideas, anyone?

01:15:09.600 --> 01:15:10.650
﻿Damn...

01:15:10.650 --> 01:15:11.730
﻿While we wait...

01:15:12.570 --> 01:15:15.070
﻿It's possible someone's out there being killed.

01:15:24.790 --> 01:15:25.580
﻿We did it!

01:15:25.580 --> 01:15:26.580
﻿It's the oak tree!

01:15:27.580 --> 01:15:28.330
﻿Huh?

01:15:28.330 --> 01:15:29.210
﻿There's another one.

01:15:29.830 --> 01:15:32.420
﻿Could it be taped up too?

01:15:35.590 --> 01:15:36.880
﻿Just a little more...

01:15:38.130 --> 01:15:40.470
It's taped, just like we expected.

01:15:48.480 --> 01:15:50.020
﻿It must be there.

01:15:50.020 --> 01:15:52.770
﻿Someone needing our help must be in there.

01:15:52.770 --> 01:15:53.400
﻿Probably.

01:15:53.770 --> 01:15:54.690
﻿But, still...

01:15:54.690 --> 01:15:56.320
﻿It's a little creepy.

01:15:56.860 --> 01:15:58.440
﻿I feel like something's coming.

01:15:58.440 --> 01:15:59.860
﻿Stop talking like that.

01:16:04.240 --> 01:16:07.830
﻿As expected at a place like this, the stars are pretty!

01:16:08.660 --> 01:16:10.500
﻿That one's Polaris...

01:16:10.500 --> 01:16:12.670
﻿And those form the Big Dipper.

01:16:16.000 --> 01:16:17.710
﻿Those shapes...

01:16:17.710 --> 01:16:19.550
﻿﻿﻿Where have I seen them...

01:16:21.970 --> 01:16:22.840
﻿What!?

01:16:22.840 --> 01:16:25.180
﻿Polaris and the Big Dipper!?

01:16:26.180 --> 01:16:30.770
Then, you're saying the crime scenes
 ﻿represent Polaris and the Big Dipper?

01:16:30.770 --> 01:16:33.230
﻿﻿﻿There's no mistaking it, Inspector!

01:16:34.310 --> 01:16:36.190
﻿You're the detective from earlier.

01:16:36.190 --> 01:16:36.690
﻿Yeah.

01:16:37.150 --> 01:16:41.990
﻿So, Mizutani-san and Honjou-san's hobby was star-gazing?

01:16:41.990 --> 01:16:42.950
﻿Thanks.

01:16:42.950 --> 01:16:43.870
﻿Superintendent!

01:16:44.320 --> 01:16:48.540
﻿The final star from the Big Dipper
﻿matches the location of Shiba Park.

01:16:48.910 --> 01:16:49.910
﻿Good work.

01:16:49.910 --> 01:16:53.250
﻿Megure, secure an emergency warrant for
﻿Mizutani Kousuke and await further orders here.

01:16:53.920 --> 01:16:56.000
﻿The rest of you, head over to Shiba Park.

01:16:56.000 --> 01:16:56.630
Hurry!

01:16:56.630 --> 01:16:57.210
﻿Yes, sir!

01:16:59.170 --> 01:17:00.170
﻿What the...

01:17:00.840 --> 01:17:02.930
﻿Don't scare us like that!

01:17:02.930 --> 01:17:04.640
﻿What do you mean by that?

01:17:05.390 --> 01:17:08.600
﻿You shouldn't be hanging around here at this hour.

01:17:09.020 --> 01:17:11.180
﻿We're not hanging around!

01:17:11.180 --> 01:17:12.480
﻿We're here to help!

01:17:12.690 --> 01:17:15.150
To help the person who used the
 ﻿beetles to send those S.O.S. messages!

01:17:15.770 --> 01:17:17.480
﻿Regardless, go home.

01:17:17.480 --> 01:17:18.650
﻿Your parents are worried about...

01:17:18.650 --> 01:17:19.530
﻿Not so fast.

01:17:21.110 --> 01:17:24.820
﻿They can go home after we answer that message.

01:17:35.670 --> 01:17:37.380
﻿Thank you very much.

01:17:48.470 --> 01:17:49.560
I'll take it.

01:17:49.560 --> 01:17:51.100
﻿Ah, sorry.

01:17:51.100 --> 01:17:51.930
﻿If you would.

01:17:54.350 --> 01:17:55.980
﻿Hello, this is Takagi's cell.

01:17:57.980 --> 01:17:58.650
﻿Agasa-san.

01:17:59.270 --> 01:18:01.110
﻿We're a little occupied here.

01:18:01.530 --> 01:18:03.530
﻿My apoIogies for disturbing you.

01:18:03.530 --> 01:18:04.990
﻿Can I tell you something?

01:18:05.360 --> 01:18:07.570
﻿This may sound strange, but...

01:18:08.740 --> 01:18:09.700
﻿The Beatles?

01:18:10.330 --> 01:18:11.040
﻿Don't tell me...

01:18:11.700 --> 01:18:12.750
﻿Understood.

01:18:12.750 --> 01:18:14.210
﻿I'll be right there.

01:18:14.210 --> 01:18:16.750
﻿Professor, hide with the kids in a safe place for now.

01:18:17.710 --> 01:18:18.250
﻿Takagi-kun...

01:18:18.790 --> 01:18:19.880
﻿Make a detour to Beika Forest.

01:18:20.500 --> 01:18:21.710
﻿But...

01:18:21.710 --> 01:18:22.630
﻿Don't worry-

01:18:22.630 --> 01:18:24.340
﻿I'll take full responsibility.

01:18:25.880 --> 01:18:27.050
﻿Understood.

01:18:27.050 --> 01:18:28.800
﻿But, allow me take that responsibility.

01:18:31.390 --> 01:18:32.350
﻿Hey, which way?

01:18:33.390 --> 01:18:34.350
﻿I dunno!

01:18:37.730 --> 01:18:38.900
﻿It's to the left.

01:18:38.900 --> 01:18:39.360
﻿Got it.

01:18:46.490 --> 01:18:47.700
Conan-kun was on TV?

01:18:48.160 --> 01:18:48.870
Yeah.

01:18:48.870 --> 01:18:51.410
﻿I saw him enter Touto Tower by himself.

01:18:51.830 --> 01:18:53.490
﻿It was around 8:00, I think.

01:18:53.490 --> 01:18:54.370
﻿I see...

01:18:54.870 --> 01:18:57.370
﻿Well, no need to worry―he'll come home soon anyway

01:18:58.040 --> 01:18:58.960
﻿But...

01:18:58.960 --> 01:19:00.880
﻿His cell phone's been turned off...

01:19:07.630 --> 01:19:09.140
﻿It's no use, Superintendent.

01:19:09.140 --> 01:19:10.390
﻿Takagi and Satou aren't answering.

01:19:11.140 --> 01:19:13.260
﻿Leave them be, then.

01:19:13.260 --> 01:19:13.640
All right.

01:19:14.310 --> 01:19:17.230
﻿Mizutani should be hiding somewhere around here.

01:19:17.230 --> 01:19:19.600
﻿Split up, and arrest him when you find him.

01:19:19.600 --> 01:19:20.150
﻿Yes, sir!

01:19:41.750 --> 01:19:43.420
﻿It's so cloudy that you can't see them.

01:19:44.670 --> 01:19:46.880
﻿The stars you and Nanako-san loved most...

01:19:48.380 --> 01:19:50.340
﻿Polaris and the Big Dipper.

01:19:51.550 --> 01:19:52.220
﻿Boy...

01:19:54.430 --> 01:19:55.600
﻿About this visitor...

01:19:56.060 --> 01:19:56.890
﻿You saw him?

01:19:57.230 --> 01:19:57.980
Yes.

01:19:57.980 --> 01:20:01.350
﻿He's visited the tower after-hours often, so I took notice.

01:20:02.020 --> 01:20:06.070
﻿Around 7:00, he went up to the viewing platform alone.

01:20:09.400 --> 01:20:12.110
﻿So you're that the assistant of that Detective Mouri.

01:20:14.200 --> 01:20:16.160
﻿But it's too bad, huh?

01:20:16.160 --> 01:20:20.160
﻿To have come so close to the sky
﻿and not be able to see the stars.

01:20:21.870 --> 01:20:23.000
﻿I can see them.

01:20:27.960 --> 01:20:29.340
﻿Whenever, wherever...

01:20:30.300 --> 01:20:32.050
Only those stars...

01:20:33.300 --> 01:20:33.800
﻿What?

01:20:33.800 --> 01:20:35.050
﻿The viewing platform?

01:20:35.050 --> 01:20:35.930
﻿Yes, sir!

01:20:35.930 --> 01:20:37.890
﻿This lady seems to have witnessed him.

01:20:38.520 --> 01:20:39.930
﻿Did you see him leave?

01:20:39.930 --> 01:20:41.350
No, I didn't.

01:20:43.150 --> 01:20:44.110
﻿All right.

01:20:44.110 --> 01:20:46.820
﻿There's no doubt that our suspect
﻿is still on the platform above.

01:20:47.570 --> 01:20:51.030
﻿He may be planning to call someone
﻿up there to commit another crime.

01:20:51.950 --> 01:20:56.780
﻿We are to ambush and arrest
﻿him while protecting the victim.

01:20:56.780 --> 01:20:59.330
﻿The suspect may be armed.

01:20:59.870 --> 01:21:00.750
﻿Stay alert and commence.

01:21:01.540 --> 01:21:04.710
﻿Please keep the interior lightings as it is.

01:21:04.710 --> 01:21:05.500
﻿Roger.

01:21:06.090 --> 01:21:06.670
﻿Go!

01:21:06.670 --> 01:21:07.170
﻿Yes, sir!

01:21:09.920 --> 01:21:11.220
﻿Hey, Mizutani-san.

01:21:14.090 --> 01:21:16.010
﻿After drinking that wine...

01:21:16.010 --> 01:21:17.140
﻿You're planning to commit suicide, right?

01:21:19.220 --> 01:21:21.350
﻿"There are eight people I cannot forgive."

01:21:21.350 --> 01:21:22.560
"﻿Now, only one remains."

01:21:23.560 --> 01:21:25.610
﻿The one that still remains...

01:21:25.610 --> 01:21:26.650
﻿Mizutani-san...

01:21:26.650 --> 01:21:27.690
﻿It's you, isn't it?

01:21:41.540 --> 01:21:47.250
﻿The shock and the anger you felt when you
﻿learned the details of Nanako-san's death...

01:21:47.250 --> 01:21:48.590
﻿I think I understand.

01:21:49.800 --> 01:21:54.010
﻿That's why you went to the hotel in Kyoto
﻿and investigated those seven people, right?

01:21:56.720 --> 01:21:58.260
﻿Just as you said...

01:21:59.600 --> 01:22:01.520
﻿On that fateful day, two years ago...

01:22:01.520 --> 01:22:04.100
﻿If I hadn't gone to meet my friend...

01:22:04.100 --> 01:22:05.810
﻿Nana wouldn't have died.

01:22:06.810 --> 01:22:08.190
﻿When I think of that...

01:22:08.190 --> 01:22:10.230
﻿I can't forgive myself.

01:22:10.900 --> 01:22:12.490
﻿But you mustn't commit suicide!

01:22:12.490 --> 01:22:14.240
﻿That just means you're murdering your―

01:22:14.240 --> 01:22:15.110
﻿I know that.

01:22:16.110 --> 01:22:17.370
﻿I know that, but...

01:22:17.700 --> 01:22:21.540
﻿I can no longer bear to live in a world without Nana...

01:22:25.120 --> 01:22:26.040
﻿Not to mention...

01:22:26.620 --> 01:22:27.960
﻿I'll get a death sentence anyway.

01:22:27.960 --> 01:22:29.290
﻿It won't be a death sentence.

01:22:31.250 --> 01:22:32.670
﻿After all, Mizutani-san...

01:22:32.670 --> 01:22:33.970
﻿You didn't kill anyone.

01:22:36.430 --> 01:22:41.470
﻿Wasn't there someone who asked you, with
﻿your kind heart, to take guilt on yourself...

01:22:41.470 --> 01:22:45.430
﻿And commit suicide in exchange for
﻿them killing those seven people?

01:22:46.230 --> 01:22:51.400
﻿I don't object to your desire to take
 ﻿responsibility for Nanako-san's death.

01:22:52.020 --> 01:22:53.150
﻿But, listen...

01:22:53.150 --> 01:22:57.070
﻿The one that other person really despises and wishes to kill...

01:22:57.070 --> 01:22:58.740
﻿Is actually you, Mizutani-san.

01:23:00.620 --> 01:23:01.200
﻿And it's because...

01:23:01.740 --> 01:23:03.120
﻿You were the one...

01:23:03.120 --> 01:23:05.160
﻿Who took away his beloved sister.

01:23:06.330 --> 01:23:07.040
﻿Isn't that right...

01:23:08.040 --> 01:23:09.420
﻿Nanako-san's elder brother...

01:23:10.250 --> 01:23:11.460
﻿Honjou Kazuki-san?

01:23:14.760 --> 01:23:15.670
﻿Brother!

01:23:15.670 --> 01:23:16.420
﻿Why are you here?

01:23:16.840 --> 01:23:19.260
﻿Bastard, you have no right to address me that way!

01:23:21.010 --> 01:23:21.600
﻿Brat...

01:23:22.300 --> 01:23:24.140
﻿How did you know I did it?

01:23:24.890 --> 01:23:27.560
﻿It made no sense, no matter how I looked at it.

01:23:28.560 --> 01:23:31.110
﻿If Mizutani-san had been the culprit...

01:23:31.110 --> 01:23:34.980
﻿The logic behind choosing the positions of
﻿Polaris and the Big Dipper as the crime scenes...

01:23:34.980 --> 01:23:36.030
﻿Wouldn't have made sense.

01:23:36.820 --> 01:23:37.820
﻿Because...

01:23:37.820 --> 01:23:39.910
﻿That would've defiled his precious stars, no?

01:23:41.950 --> 01:23:44.660
﻿As such, I thought this may have been...

01:23:44.660 --> 01:23:49.420
﻿A plan someone else had come up with, in order to
﻿make the star-loving Mizutani-san their scapegoat.

01:23:50.170 --> 01:23:52.380
﻿When I realized that, everything came together.

01:23:53.210 --> 01:23:54.340
﻿Moreover...

01:23:54.340 --> 01:23:58.760
﻿The culprit, who accurately adapted the positions
 ﻿of Polaris and the Big Dipper to the map...

01:23:58.760 --> 01:24:02.010
And used them for crime scenes,
 ﻿was clearly a perfectionist.

01:24:03.100 --> 01:24:05.510
﻿But, the sign oh Mizutani-san's apartment door...

01:24:05.970 --> 01:24:07.520
﻿Was slightly tilted...

01:24:07.520 --> 01:24:09.810
﻿And the handwriting wasn't very tidy either.

01:24:10.350 --> 01:24:11.520
﻿By comparison...

01:24:11.520 --> 01:24:13.770
﻿The phone number written on your name card...

01:24:14.820 --> 01:24:16.820
﻿Was in very neat handwriting.

01:24:16.820 --> 01:24:19.740
﻿There was even a faint pencil line,
﻿to ensure the writing was straight.

01:24:20.530 --> 01:24:22.200
﻿And inside your organizer...

01:24:22.200 --> 01:24:25.660
﻿Even the names and addresses of those
﻿that sent flowers were clearly recorded.

01:24:26.450 --> 01:24:30.120
﻿All of this undeniably showcases your
﻿perfectionist personality, doesn't it?

01:24:31.500 --> 01:24:32.500
﻿You...

01:24:32.500 --> 01:24:34.000
﻿Just who are you, really?

01:24:34.710 --> 01:24:35.800
﻿Edogawa Conan.

01:24:36.500 --> 01:24:37.460
﻿A detective.

01:24:42.260 --> 01:24:43.340
﻿Thanks for coming.

01:24:44.010 --> 01:24:44.890
﻿Agasa-san...

01:24:44.890 --> 01:24:46.220
﻿Where are the other kids?

01:24:46.680 --> 01:24:48.770
﻿Their parents took them home.

01:24:49.520 --> 01:24:50.600
﻿I'll show you the way.

01:24:51.020 --> 01:24:52.060
﻿Please do.

01:24:56.650 --> 01:24:58.190
﻿Ai-kun, go wait in the car.

01:25:00.780 --> 01:25:04.660
﻿The one who told Mizutani-san the
﻿whole story of how Nanako-san died...

01:25:04.660 --> 01:25:05.450
﻿It was you, wasn't it?

01:25:06.120 --> 01:25:06.580
﻿Yeah.

01:25:06.990 --> 01:25:07.950
﻿That day...

01:25:07.950 --> 01:25:13.750
﻿When I heard from this guy that Shindou Sumire, the
﻿artist, was staying in the same hotel on the same floor...

01:25:14.880 --> 01:25:18.000
﻿I went to her personal art exhibition to ask some questions.

01:25:18.380 --> 01:25:23.260
﻿At that time, I happened to overhear Sumire and Ryuuzaki talking.

01:25:24.720 --> 01:25:27.350
﻿And you passed on the information to Mizutani-san...

01:25:27.350 --> 01:25:28.930
﻿While adding in your own lies.

01:25:29.640 --> 01:25:31.890
﻿On the first anniversary of Nanako-san's death...

01:25:31.890 --> 01:25:35.560
﻿Everyone who had been on the 6th floor brought flowers.

01:25:36.480 --> 01:25:40.480
﻿If it was because they felt guilty, only
﻿one or two might have come, but...

01:25:40.480 --> 01:25:42.610
﻿All seven came.

01:25:42.610 --> 01:25:45.910
﻿The only possible reason for that was
 ﻿they wanted to express their gratitude.

01:25:46.910 --> 01:25:51.370
They wanted to say, "Thank you," for
 ﻿allowing them to board the elevator.

01:25:52.330 --> 01:25:53.790
T﻿hen, could it be...

01:25:53.790 --> 01:25:55.830
﻿Nanako wasn't chased out...

01:25:55.830 --> 01:25:57.000
﻿But instead voluntarily...

01:25:59.210 --> 01:26:00.960
﻿Yeah, that's right.

01:26:00.960 --> 01:26:03.170
﻿Nanako was that kind of a girl.

01:26:03.720 --> 01:26:04.840
﻿But even still!

01:26:04.840 --> 01:26:09.720
That doesn't change the fact that it was because
 ﻿of them boarding that elevator that she died!

01:26:11.970 --> 01:26:13.350
﻿Mizutani-san...

01:26:14.060 --> 01:26:18.980
﻿Indeed, Nanako-san did die in place of those seven people.

01:26:19.570 --> 01:26:20.270
﻿However...

01:26:20.940 --> 01:26:22.650
﻿Even though you're also a substitute...

01:26:22.650 --> 01:26:26.950
﻿By taking Honjou-san's place and
﻿killing yourself to atone for his sins...

01:26:26.950 --> 01:26:29.030
﻿There's a world of difference there!

01:26:29.450 --> 01:26:30.990
﻿And that difference...

01:26:30.990 --> 01:26:35.290
﻿Is as great as that of a star in the sky
 ﻿and a stone rolling on the ground.

01:26:44.170 --> 01:26:44.760
﻿Nana...

01:26:48.090 --> 01:26:48.970
﻿I quit.

01:26:48.970 --> 01:26:49.430
﻿What?

01:26:50.390 --> 01:26:51.560
﻿I'm sorry.

01:26:51.560 --> 01:26:53.140
﻿I won't be committing suicide.

01:26:53.810 --> 01:26:55.890
﻿This boy's words brought me to my senses.

01:26:57.770 --> 01:26:58.600
﻿Mizutani!

01:26:58.730 --> 01:27:00.810
﻿And, I'm sure that Nana in heaven...

01:27:02.820 --> 01:27:05.820
﻿Wouldn't want me to commit suicide either.

01:27:06.780 --> 01:27:07.780
﻿I'm returning this to you.

01:27:08.660 --> 01:27:10.410
﻿I have no need for it now.

01:27:11.830 --> 01:27:13.830
﻿Please turn yourself in, Brother.

01:27:14.290 --> 01:27:15.080
Damn!

01:27:15.830 --> 01:27:16.790
﻿Honjou-san.

01:27:17.370 --> 01:27:20.540
﻿Those are the items you took from the seven victims, right?

01:27:21.460 --> 01:27:24.800
﻿You handed these to him and assured
﻿him that, if he died with these on him...

01:27:24.800 --> 01:27:26.420
﻿He would be presumed the murderer, right?

01:27:28.050 --> 01:27:29.760
﻿It's a good thing I came.

01:27:30.680 --> 01:27:33.220
﻿When I heard that Detective Mouri was investigating...

01:27:33.220 --> 01:27:35.720
﻿I rushed here fearing I would be exposed.

01:27:36.680 --> 01:27:38.730
﻿I lied to you because...

01:27:38.730 --> 01:27:42.110
﻿I was hoping you would be the one taking revenge on them.

01:27:42.110 --> 01:27:44.070
﻿But you didn't have the courage to do so.

01:27:45.030 --> 01:27:46.780
﻿That's why I had to do it myself!

01:27:47.240 --> 01:27:48.820
﻿That isn't courage!

01:27:48.820 --> 01:27:50.160
﻿It's merely self-satisfaction!

01:27:50.160 --> 01:27:50.570
﻿Shut up!

01:27:51.530 --> 01:27:54.490
﻿Since Detective Mouri isn't here, that must mean you came alone!

01:27:55.410 --> 01:27:56.410
﻿Don't belittle me!

01:28:03.790 --> 01:28:05.130
﻿Did I make it in time?

01:28:06.550 --> 01:28:08.260
﻿I'm Matsumoto from the Police Headquarters.

01:28:09.260 --> 01:28:10.010
﻿Police Headquarters?

01:28:10.680 --> 01:28:12.640
﻿Are you injured?

01:28:15.640 --> 01:28:17.180
﻿Come with me to the station.

01:28:23.020 --> 01:28:23.730
﻿Damn it!

01:28:25.110 --> 01:28:25.980
﻿Shit!

01:28:26.400 --> 01:28:27.570
﻿Like I'd be caught by the likes of you!

01:28:36.240 --> 01:28:37.620
A﻿s I thought, you...

01:28:38.450 --> 01:28:40.580
﻿You're Irish, aren't you?

01:28:46.960 --> 01:28:47.710
﻿Police!

01:28:47.710 --> 01:28:48.460
﻿Don't move!

01:28:51.300 --> 01:28:52.430
﻿As expected!

01:28:52.430 --> 01:28:53.010
﻿Superintendent!

01:28:53.390 --> 01:28:54.350
﻿Superintendent!?

01:28:58.970 --> 01:29:00.140
﻿Please be strong!

01:29:00.680 --> 01:29:01.980
﻿Superintendent!

01:29:01.980 --> 01:29:02.900
﻿What're you doing here?

01:29:03.350 --> 01:29:05.520
﻿The other Superintendent Matsumoto is a fake!

01:29:05.520 --> 01:29:06.520
﻿He's been replaced!

01:29:07.940 --> 01:29:10.070
﻿The superintendent was from The Beatles generation.

01:29:10.070 --> 01:29:12.150
﻿But I never thought it'd really be him...

01:29:12.820 --> 01:29:13.990
﻿Hurry and contact Inspector Megure!

01:29:14.990 --> 01:29:15.370
﻿Roger!

01:29:20.870 --> 01:29:21.790
It's me.

01:29:21.790 --> 01:29:22.460
﻿What is it?

01:29:23.080 --> 01:29:24.670
﻿We've been exposed.

01:29:24.670 --> 01:29:26.420
﻿They know he's a fake.

01:29:27.540 --> 01:29:28.420
﻿Got it.

01:29:50.940 --> 01:29:52.190
﻿Vermouth...

01:29:58.450 --> 01:29:59.660
﻿He really was here?

01:30:00.200 --> 01:30:01.040
﻿Yeah.

01:30:01.040 --> 01:30:02.870
﻿He left his skateboard in my care...

01:30:02.870 --> 01:30:06.170
﻿But since he never retrieved it, I thought it was strange.

01:30:06.170 --> 01:30:08.130
﻿Surely he isn't still in there!

01:30:08.670 --> 01:30:10.250
﻿That can't be.

01:30:10.800 --> 01:30:12.090
﻿It would be disastrous if he were.

01:30:12.090 --> 01:30:14.090
﻿He could run into that murderer!

01:30:15.050 --> 01:30:16.050
﻿Murderer!?

01:30:16.640 --> 01:30:19.510
﻿The police are conducting a search inside right now.

01:30:19.510 --> 01:30:20.720
﻿Sonoko, wait here!

01:30:21.470 --> 01:30:21.930
﻿Wait, Ran!

01:30:22.310 --> 01:30:23.890
﻿Hey, you! Wait!

01:30:28.480 --> 01:30:30.440
﻿What have you done with Superintendent Matsumoto?

01:30:31.690 --> 01:30:32.440
﻿Don't tell me...

01:30:33.280 --> 01:30:35.150
﻿Nah, he's still alive.

01:30:35.570 --> 01:30:40.030
﻿I need him to be my scapegoat, you know.

01:30:42.040 --> 01:30:45.330
﻿I'm assuming that’s the memory card
﻿containing the Organization's NOC list?

01:30:45.710 --> 01:30:46.420
﻿Yeah.

01:30:46.420 --> 01:30:47.250
﻿Might be.

01:30:48.790 --> 01:30:51.300
﻿When did you find out I was a fake?

01:30:52.380 --> 01:30:55.010
﻿I had a general idea.

01:30:55.010 --> 01:30:57.510
﻿If Vermouth, the master of disguise...

01:30:57.510 --> 01:31:00.260
﻿Had sent someone else to infiltrate in her stead...

01:31:00.260 --> 01:31:03.100
﻿That could have been made impossible
﻿due to the difference in body stature.

01:31:03.770 --> 01:31:05.270
﻿And when I thought along those lines...

01:31:05.270 --> 01:31:07.060
﻿You were the first to come to mind.

01:31:08.270 --> 01:31:09.350
I see.

01:31:09.860 --> 01:31:10.810
﻿As expected...

01:31:10.810 --> 01:31:11.940
﻿Of Kudou Shinichi.

01:31:13.360 --> 01:31:17.070
﻿Before matching the fingerprints, I was skeptical too.

01:31:18.490 --> 01:31:20.700
﻿Have you already reported this to your boss?

01:31:20.870 --> 01:31:22.330
﻿No, not yet.

01:31:22.950 --> 01:31:24.950
﻿I haven't told anyone.

01:31:26.620 --> 01:31:27.620
﻿Not even Gin?

01:31:28.290 --> 01:31:29.040
﻿Yeah.

01:31:29.290 --> 01:31:31.210
﻿About Kudou Shinichi.

01:31:31.210 --> 01:31:32.460
﻿Have you forgotten?

01:31:33.920 --> 01:31:35.880
﻿I've done away with a lot of people.

01:31:35.880 --> 01:31:37.930
﻿How could I possibly remember them all?

01:31:38.340 --> 01:31:40.090
﻿What is it about this one?

01:31:41.890 --> 01:31:42.640
﻿No.

01:31:42.640 --> 01:31:44.010
﻿It's nothing.

01:31:44.720 --> 01:31:46.350
﻿Regardless, concentrate on your assignment.

01:31:50.730 --> 01:31:51.520
﻿Why?

01:31:54.230 --> 01:31:55.530
﻿There was a time when...

01:31:55.610 --> 01:31:58.700
﻿He shot a fellow member of the
﻿Organization that made a mistake.

01:31:58.700 --> 01:32:02.490
﻿He left the body to burn there at Haido City Hotel...

01:32:02.490 --> 01:32:03.910
﻿Where it eventually turned to ashes.

01:32:09.080 --> 01:32:13.460
﻿That member was someone I respected like a father.

01:32:15.250 --> 01:32:17.050
﻿Haido City Hotel...

01:32:20.180 --> 01:32:20.970
﻿Pisco!?

01:32:23.930 --> 01:32:26.430
﻿You've investigated us thoroughly, haven't you?

01:32:26.930 --> 01:32:29.430
﻿To have failed in killing Kudou Shinichi...

01:32:29.430 --> 01:32:32.270
﻿And then failing to see through to your true identity...

01:32:32.270 --> 01:32:33.860
﻿He's made a huge oversight.

01:32:35.480 --> 01:32:38.440
﻿I'll be taking you to meet <i>that</i> person...

01:32:39.280 --> 01:32:43.910
﻿To have you act as a witness in order to overthrow
﻿that conceited and cold-blooded bastard.

01:32:44.740 --> 01:32:47.870
﻿Only this man is sure of my identity as of now...

01:32:48.450 --> 01:32:50.120
﻿As long as I can defeat him...

01:32:50.870 --> 01:32:53.040
﻿But, with the tranquilizer out of action...

01:32:54.500 --> 01:32:55.460
﻿There's only...

01:33:01.050 --> 01:33:02.590
﻿Have no fear.

01:33:02.590 --> 01:33:03.760
I won't kill you.

01:33:04.430 --> 01:33:06.350
﻿I'm just going to knock you unconscious.

01:33:08.180 --> 01:33:10.480
﻿Unless I bring you back alive...

01:33:10.480 --> 01:33:13.980
I should think you being Kudou
Shinichi is something <i>that</i> person...

01:33:13.980 --> 01:33:16.360
﻿Would find hard to believe.

01:33:24.490 --> 01:33:25.620
﻿This is...

01:33:25.950 --> 01:33:26.910
﻿Detective Chiba?

01:33:29.120 --> 01:33:30.120
﻿Detective Chiba!

01:33:30.120 --> 01:33:31.080
﻿Are you all right?

01:33:34.370 --> 01:33:35.880
﻿It seems he's just lost consciousness...

01:33:36.630 --> 01:33:38.000
﻿I think the same goes for the rest of them, too...

01:33:39.840 --> 01:33:40.630
﻿Conan-kun!

01:33:41.550 --> 01:33:42.340
﻿Hey, you!

01:33:44.470 --> 01:33:45.510
﻿You, wait up!

01:33:51.390 --> 01:33:52.060
﻿Conan-kun!

01:33:54.100 --> 01:33:54.900
﻿Conan-kun!

01:33:55.190 --> 01:33:56.270
﻿What happened?

01:33:57.610 --> 01:33:58.360
﻿Ran...neechan...

01:33:58.360 --> 01:33:59.360
﻿Are you all right?

01:33:59.360 --> 01:34:00.610
﻿Are the two of you all right?

01:34:01.940 --> 01:34:03.280
﻿Detective Matsumoto!

01:34:04.030 --> 01:34:04.910
﻿It's serious!

01:34:04.910 --> 01:34:06.530
﻿The other detectives downstairs were...

01:34:08.080 --> 01:34:09.280
﻿Attacked by the culprit?

01:34:11.870 --> 01:34:12.700
﻿What is it?

01:34:13.330 --> 01:34:14.410
﻿No good...

01:34:14.410 --> 01:34:15.000
﻿Run...

01:34:15.670 --> 01:34:16.500
﻿What?

01:34:16.500 --> 01:34:17.290
﻿What happened?

01:34:18.250 --> 01:34:19.170
﻿Run...

01:34:19.170 --> 01:34:19.750
He's...

01:34:28.220 --> 01:34:29.390
﻿You...

01:34:29.390 --> 01:34:31.010
﻿You aren't Superintendent Matsumoto, are you?

01:34:38.440 --> 01:34:39.270
﻿Don't...

01:34:39.730 --> 01:34:40.730
﻿It's all right.

01:34:41.900 --> 01:34:44.780
﻿I can't avoid a bullet from a rifle like Kyougoku-san, but...

01:34:45.400 --> 01:34:46.320
A ﻿pistol...

01:34:47.490 --> 01:34:48.570
﻿Say, Ran...

01:34:48.570 --> 01:34:49.410
﻿Did you know?

01:34:50.030 --> 01:34:53.540
﻿The speed of a rifle bullet is about 1000 meters per second.

01:34:54.330 --> 01:34:55.500
﻿Compared to that...

01:34:55.500 --> 01:34:57.870
﻿The speed of a pistol's bullet is only a third of that...

01:34:57.870 --> 01:35:00.840
﻿Which puts them at roughly 350 meters a second.

01:35:03.550 --> 01:35:04.590
﻿What's so funny?

01:35:05.380 --> 01:35:08.140
﻿Don't tell me that you think you can dodge a bullet?

01:35:08.970 --> 01:35:09.890
﻿That's exactly it.

01:35:10.510 --> 01:35:12.100
﻿Interesting.

01:35:12.100 --> 01:35:12.850
﻿Let's give it a try.

01:35:34.080 --> 01:35:35.410
﻿Amazing...

01:35:36.120 --> 01:35:37.750
﻿I have to hand it to you, little lady.

01:35:38.500 --> 01:35:39.880
﻿I had forgotten...

01:35:40.540 --> 01:35:43.920
﻿That you're a karate expert.

01:36:15.990 --> 01:36:16.450
﻿Ran!

01:36:24.880 --> 01:36:26.300
﻿You're really wasting my energy here.

01:36:28.090 --> 01:36:28.800
﻿Ran!

01:36:28.800 --> 01:36:29.630
﻿Stay down!

01:36:30.760 --> 01:36:32.590
Leave the rest to me.

01:36:32.590 --> 01:36:33.890
﻿Just stay there!

01:36:34.180 --> 01:36:35.560
﻿Damn...

01:36:54.320 --> 01:36:56.370
﻿Allow me to enjoy this even more!

01:37:20.060 --> 01:37:20.770
﻿Shit!

01:37:24.270 --> 01:37:25.480
﻿What a pity.

01:37:25.480 --> 01:37:26.730
﻿You were so close there.

01:37:34.950 --> 01:37:35.910
﻿What's wrong?

01:37:35.910 --> 01:37:37.030
﻿Already out of ideas?

01:37:40.500 --> 01:37:42.210
﻿Yeah, that's the way.

01:37:55.760 --> 01:37:58.640
﻿Let's end this game of cat-and-mouse, shall we?

01:38:09.230 --> 01:38:10.730
﻿How the tables have turned.

01:38:12.490 --> 01:38:13.070
﻿Shit...

01:38:13.490 --> 01:38:14.240
﻿Now...

01:38:14.240 --> 01:38:16.030
﻿Hand over the memory card!

01:38:22.160 --> 01:38:23.200
﻿They're here, huh?

01:38:33.470 --> 01:38:35.550
﻿"How the tables have turned," was it?

01:38:44.310 --> 01:38:44.980
﻿It's me.

01:38:45.890 --> 01:38:46.520
How is it?

01:38:47.020 --> 01:38:49.060
﻿Have you secured the memory card?

01:38:49.060 --> 01:38:49.860
﻿Yeah.

01:38:57.780 --> 01:38:59.200
I can't really see you.

01:38:59.950 --> 01:39:01.660
﻿Hold it out further.

01:39:05.080 --> 01:39:06.120
﻿That's right.

01:39:06.120 --> 01:39:07.120
﻿A little more.

01:39:09.580 --> 01:39:09.830
Now!

01:39:18.720 --> 01:39:20.100
﻿Bingo!

01:39:20.100 --> 01:39:22.100
﻿I wanted to shoot

01:39:23.220 --> 01:39:24.430
﻿Partner...

01:39:24.430 --> 01:39:26.430
﻿Look below.

01:39:27.020 --> 01:39:27.890
﻿That's...

01:39:28.310 --> 01:39:29.900
﻿He has no means of escape.

01:39:30.480 --> 01:39:32.860
﻿Thanks for your service, Irish.

01:39:37.150 --> 01:39:38.610
﻿There's someone else down there!

01:39:40.280 --> 01:39:41.530
﻿Hey, pull yourself together!

01:39:41.530 --> 01:39:42.080
﻿Wake up, come on!

01:39:45.540 --> 01:39:46.870
﻿It's all right!

01:39:46.870 --> 01:39:48.000
﻿It didn't hit your vital points!

01:39:48.750 --> 01:39:50.170
﻿Once we take care of them...

01:39:50.170 --> 01:39:51.380
﻿I'll hurry and get you medical treatment!

01:39:51.710 --> 01:39:53.090
﻿I see now...

01:39:56.300 --> 01:39:59.050
No wonder Vermouth thought so highly of you...

01:39:58.840 --> 01:39:59.800
Don't talk.

01:40:00.260 --> 01:40:01.930
﻿After you've recovered...

01:40:01.930 --> 01:40:04.390
﻿I'll make you reveal your boss's true identity, so be prepared!

01:40:13.060 --> 01:40:13.650
﻿Irish!

01:40:14.900 --> 01:40:16.440
﻿Kudou Shinichi...

01:40:16.820 --> 01:40:19.490
﻿Keep... coming after us...

01:40:21.030 --> 01:40:21.700
﻿Irish!

01:40:22.990 --> 01:40:24.530
﻿They used Irish as a shield!

01:40:25.620 --> 01:40:27.660
﻿It'll be troublesome if we have to land.

01:40:27.660 --> 01:40:29.120
﻿Use that!

01:40:29.120 --> 01:40:29.620
﻿Roger!

01:40:34.250 --> 01:40:35.210
Damn it!

01:40:51.850 --> 01:40:52.650
﻿This is bad...

01:40:52.650 --> 01:40:53.900
﻿Ran's still downstairs!

01:41:00.610 --> 01:41:01.490
There we go.

01:41:01.490 --> 01:41:01.910
﻿Continue!

01:41:35.400 --> 01:41:36.270
﻿Partner...

01:41:36.270 --> 01:41:37.190
﻿What should we do?

01:41:38.110 --> 01:41:38.820
﻿Chianti...

01:41:38.820 --> 01:41:39.530
﻿Smoke them out.

01:41:40.110 --> 01:41:40.990
OK.

01:41:41.570 --> 01:41:42.780
﻿Damn it...

01:41:42.780 --> 01:41:43.360
﻿What now!?

01:41:47.280 --> 01:41:48.030
﻿Tear gas!

01:41:51.290 --> 01:41:52.080
﻿There we are.

01:41:53.080 --> 01:41:54.920
﻿Force them to the top!

01:42:19.900 --> 01:42:21.190
﻿The mouse has been cornered.

01:42:22.320 --> 01:42:22.940
﻿Go up.

01:42:22.940 --> 01:42:23.780
﻿Attack from above!

01:42:24.240 --> 01:42:26.200
﻿There'll be nowhere to hide!

01:42:26.200 --> 01:42:26.910
﻿Roger!

01:42:33.960 --> 01:42:34.580
﻿Damn...

01:42:35.000 --> 01:42:35.960
What do I do...

01:42:35.960 --> 01:42:37.880
﻿If this goes on, I'll be a sitting duck!

01:42:41.420 --> 01:42:42.130
Damn it!

01:42:42.130 --> 01:42:42.920
What do I do?

01:43:05.320 --> 01:43:06.240
Now...

01:43:06.240 --> 01:43:08.110
Let's see your face.

01:43:20.880 --> 01:43:22.000
﻿They just jumped!

01:43:23.340 --> 01:43:24.960
﻿Accepting their fate of no escape, huh?

01:43:34.680 --> 01:43:35.890
﻿Go!

01:43:49.490 --> 01:43:50.410
﻿We've been hit!

01:43:50.660 --> 01:43:51.410
﻿Great!

01:43:51.410 --> 01:43:52.200
﻿Now what!?

01:43:53.030 --> 01:43:54.580
﻿I can't control it anymore!

01:43:54.580 --> 01:43:55.330
﻿We have no choice!

01:43:55.330 --> 01:43:56.080
﻿Retreat!

01:43:56.500 --> 01:43:57.160
﻿Roger!

01:43:57.750 --> 01:43:58.620
Who...

01:44:01.960 --> 01:44:03.800
﻿Who the hell was that?

01:44:26.480 --> 01:44:28.610
﻿As expected of the Silver Bullet.

01:44:28.860 --> 01:44:30.030
﻿He has his ways.

01:44:37.250 --> 01:44:38.790
﻿Actually, about that...

01:44:38.790 --> 01:44:42.250
﻿There was a huge bang and I fainted.

01:44:42.460 --> 01:44:44.340
﻿Thank goodness no one was hurt.

01:44:44.340 --> 01:44:45.210
﻿I'm sorry!

01:44:46.340 --> 01:44:47.170
﻿Well then, Ran-chan.

01:44:47.800 --> 01:44:50.760
﻿I'll inquire as to the details another day.

01:44:50.760 --> 01:44:52.260
﻿Thanks in advance.

01:44:52.260 --> 01:44:53.300
﻿Sure.

01:44:53.300 --> 01:44:55.720
﻿I'll arrange for a car to send you home now.

01:44:55.720 --> 01:44:56.850
﻿Please wait a while.

01:44:57.310 --> 01:44:58.730
﻿Thank you very much.

01:45:00.270 --> 01:45:01.600
﻿Are you really all right?

01:45:02.650 --> 01:45:05.400
﻿Oh yeah, I'll get you something to drink.

01:45:05.400 --> 01:45:06.650
﻿You don't have to...

01:45:06.980 --> 01:45:09.030
﻿Don't mention it.

01:45:09.030 --> 01:45:10.240
﻿Thanks.

01:45:10.240 --> 01:45:11.400
﻿Ran-neechan...

01:45:12.820 --> 01:45:17.120
﻿Shinichi-niichan said that the case has been solved.

01:45:18.160 --> 01:45:19.330
﻿Come to think of it, Shinichi...

01:45:19.910 --> 01:45:22.710
﻿About that, he said he had another case...

01:45:24.040 --> 01:45:26.170
﻿He left abruptly again?

01:45:26.750 --> 01:45:28.170
﻿And...

01:45:28.170 --> 01:45:32.050
﻿I'm sure he said something like
"﻿Don't tell anyone I was involved."

01:45:35.510 --> 01:45:36.800
